<title>JAPAN: Japan financial issues firm on short-covering.</title>
<headline>Japan financial issues firm on short-covering.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese financial sector issues firmed in the Thursday morning session on short-covering, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0146 GMT, Sumitomo Bank Ltd was up 90 yen at 1,770, in trade totalling 3.9 million issues. It was the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd rose 15 yen to 778. It was the third most heavily traded issue with 2.54 million shares traded.</p>
<p>Nomura Securities Co Ltd climbed 40 yen to 1,430.</p>
</text>
